  "issue_date": "2025-12-19",
  "report_week": "51",
  "report_period": "Week 51 (12th Dec to 19th Dec 2025)",
  "commentary": {
    "bulkers": "Zodiac Maritime have committed their Newcastlemax \"Cape Merlin\" 206/2005 Imabari, Japan (SS/DD 02/2026) to Chinese interests at USD 23,5 mill. Remind you that a month ago, the one-year-younger sister vessel \"Seacon Africa\" 206/2006 Imabari, Japan (SS/DD 06/2026) was sold at USD 22,7 mill. Following the sale of the Kamsarmax \"Theresa Hebei\" 81/2012 Sainty, China (SS/DD 03/2027) in November at USD 15,5 mill, Raffles Shipping have now committed the one-year-younger sister vessel \"Theresa Hainan\" 81/2013 Sainty, China (SS/DD 05/2028) at low-mid USD 16 mill. Oasis Ship Management have committed the Panamax \"The Giver\" 75/2006 Sanoyas, Japan (SS 03/2030, DD 06/2028) to Chinese interests at USD 11,2 mill. Note that the sister vessel \"Yasa Unity\" 75/2006 Sanoyas, Japan (SS/DD 04/2026) was sold in November at mid USD 9 mill. On the Supramax sector, LA Maritime committed the \"Captain Karam\" 56/2006 Mitsui, Japan (SS 05/2029, DD 05/2027) to Chinese interests at USD 11,25 mill. Remind you that the one-year-younger sister vessel \"Icarius\" 56/2007 Mitsui, Japan (SS/DD 04/2027) was sold back in October at USD 11,75 mill. Moreover, Precious Shipping committed their \"Wariya Naree\" 53/2011 Hindustan, India (SS/DD 02/2026) at USD 9,85 mill, while the one- year-older sister vessel \"Warisa Naree\" 53/2010 Hindustan, India (SS 04/2030, DD 01/2028) was sold earlier this month at USD 9,4 mill. Empire Bulkers have committed the Handysize \"Aphrodite M\" 34/2011 Spp, Korea (SS/DD 10/2026) to undisclosed interests at USD 12,5 mill. For comparison, the one-year-younger sister vessel \"Union Groove\" 35/2012 Spp, Korea (SS/DD 01/2027) was sold a couple of weeks ago at USD 13,6 mill.",
    "tankers": "The Suezmax \"Los Angeles Spirit\" 159/2007 Hyundai Samho, Korea (SS/DD 01/2027) of Teekay Corp was committed at mid USD 30's mill. Note that the \"Sonangol Namibe\" 158/2007 Daewoo, Korea (SS/DD 03/2027) was sold in November at USD 34 mill. Bihar International committed the Aframax \"Liana\" 106/2003 Tsuneishi, Japan (SS 11/2028, DD 02/2027) at USD 20 mill. Remind you that back in October, the one-year-younger \"Hydra\" 105/2004 Sumitomo, Japan (SS 12/2027, DD 12/2025) was sold at USD 20,75 mill. Pan Ocean's MR2 \"Grand Ace9\" 46/2008 Stx, Korea (SS 03/2028, DD 03/2026) was committed to undisclosed interests at mid USD 15 mill. For reference, the \"Falcon Royal\" 47/2008 Hyundai Mipo, Korea (SS 12/2028, DD 04/2026) was sold back in October at USD 16,5 mill.",
    "freight": {
      "Capesize": "at the level of low/mid usd 10,00's fio range. No period activity to report here.",
      "Kamsarmax / Panamax": "North Pacific rounds ranged at the usd 11,000/13,000 pd. A number of Indonesian and Australian trips into China were reported fixed in the usd 8,000/11,000 pd range. A number of Indonesian and Australian trips into India were reported at the level of usd 11,000/13,000 pd. South East Asian trips via South America into China were fixed around usd 11,000/13,000 pd. Indian trips via South Africa into India were reported at the level of usd 13,000/15,000 pd. Continental trips via US Gulf into China were fixed around usd 19,000/22,000 pd. East Coast South American trips into China were reported at the level of usd 14,000/16,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 400K/600K. No period activity to report here.",
      "Ultramax / Supramax": "Trips from North China into Arabian Gulf were reported fixed in the usd 12,000/14,000 pd range. A number of Indonesian trips into China were fixed around usd 10,000/12,000 pd. West Coast Indian trips via Arabian Gulf into East Coast India were reported at the level of usd 15,000/17,000 pd. Continental trips into Mediterranean were fixed around usd 19,000/21,000 pd. East Coast South American trips into India were reported at the level of usd 15,000/16,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 500K/600K. No period activity to report here.",
      "Handymax / Handysize": "Trips from North China via Japan into West Coast Central America were fixed around usd 8,000/11,000 pd. North Chinese trips via East Coast India into South East Asia were reported at the level of usd 8,000/10,000 pd. A number of Indonesian and Australian trips into China were reported fixed in the usd 9,000/12,000 pd range. Australian trips into Continent were fixed around usd 13,000/15,000 pd. Trips from Black Sea into Continent-Mediterranean range were reported at the level of usd 12,000/13,000 pd. Mediterranean trips into US Gulf were fixed around usd 11,000/12,000 pd. Continental trips into Australia were reported at the level of usd 14,000/16,000 pd. East Coast South American trips into Continent-Mediterranean range were fixed around usd 18,000/21,000 pd. East Coast South American coastal trips were reported at the level of usd 16,000/18,000 pd. No period activity to report here."
    }
  },
